      "title": "Why Deno?",
      "lectureOrder": 517,
      "videoOrder": 458,
      "sourceHash": "44dc608709bfd6a24b44ada661a7e7b3cb7fa7e946ed1d4895de02e7bddd86c0",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.4,
          "end": 6.27,
          "en": "Now why do we have and need Deno?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 6.27,
          "end": 8.14,
          "en": "Well, if we need it or not is, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.14,
          "end": 10.69,
          "en": "up to you and the entire community to decide.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.69,
          "end": 15.69,
          "en": "We have it because Ryan Dahl, the creator of Node,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.79,
          "end": 19.68,
          "en": "so the person who invented Node 10 years ago,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.68,
          "end": 21.81,
          "en": "is also the creator of Deno.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.81,
          "end": 24.68,
          "en": "And he came up with Deno, because he simply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.68,
          "end": 27.6,
          "en": "wasn't happy with Node anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.6,
          "end": 29.53,
          "en": "Now I wanna be very clear.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.53,
          "end": 32.91,
          "en": "Node is not going to go anywhere.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.91,
          "end": 34.75,
          "en": "And you don't need to take this from me,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.75,
          "end": 37.28,
          "en": "you can take it from Ryan himself.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.28,
          "end": 39.05,
          "en": "Node is not going anywhere.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.05,
          "end": 42.49,
          "en": "It's mature, it's big, it's there, it's established,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.49,
          "end": 45.67,
          "en": "it's being used by thousands of developers and companies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.67,
          "end": 47.98,
          "en": "So Node isn't going anywhere.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.98,
          "end": 50.9,
          "en": "But Deno can be worth a look,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.9,
          "end": 54.74,
          "en": "because it does some small things differently than Node,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.74,
          "end": 57.39,
          "en": "simply because Ryan thought like,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.39,
          "end": 60.85,
          "en": "well there was this chance of making Node better.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.85,
          "end": 63.66,
          "en": "And Deno is the result of that, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.66,
          "end": 65.35,
          "en": "Now, we'll come back to this question",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.35,
          "end": 68.5,
          "en": "of whether you wanna progress with Deno, Deno,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.5,
          "end": 69.68,
          "en": "whatever you wanna call it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.68,
          "end": 73.01,
          "en": "or if you should stick to Node at the end of the module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.01,
          "end": 74.65,
          "en": "I'll come back to that there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 74.65,
          "end": 75.8,
          "en": "The main takeaway is that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 75.8,
          "end": 77.41,
          "en": "there will be some core differences,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 77.41,
          "end": 79.64,
          "en": "which we'll see in action throughout this module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 79.64,
          "end": 80.53,
          "en": "but that, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 80.53,
          "end": 83.66,
          "en": "you might not need all those enhancements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 83.66,
          "end": 85.09,
          "en": "introduced by Deno.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 85.09,
          "end": 89.28999999999999,
          "en": "So therefore, the established, highly active ecosystem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 89.28999999999999,
          "end": 91.74,
          "en": "the fact that it's production-proved",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 91.74,
          "end": 93.27000000000001,
          "en": "and that it's very mature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 93.27000000000001,
          "end": 95.973,
          "en": "that might be strong reasons for sticking to Node.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 96.82,
          "end": 99.27000000000001,
          "en": "Deno, of course, has some core differences,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 99.27000000000001,
          "end": 100.89,
          "en": "which also might be interesting,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 100.89,
          "end": 103.08,
          "en": "and therefore, we'll now have a look at all of that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 103.08,
          "end": 104.24000000000001,
          "en": "throughout this module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 104.24000000000001,
          "end": 106.53,
          "en": "We'll get started by installing Deno,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 106.53,
          "end": 108.44,
          "en": "and by writing some basic code with it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 108.44,
